Modifications: SKILL.md was rewritten. From awesome-gamedev-agent-skills it
keeps the SceneTree runner, the --import step and the assert(), quit() and
await pitfalls (rechecked by running them with Godot 4.7.2 on 2026-10-17;
the helper is renamed check_eq). From GodotPrompter it keeps only the GUT vs
gdUnit4 comparison and rule of thumb, the unit/integration layout, the naming
rules and the "what not to test" list, with corrections: gdUnit4's CLI is
addons/gdUnit4/runtest.sh (GdUnitCmdTool.gd), not a "gdunit4_runner";
gdUnit4 finds suites by base class and generates <name>_test.gd; GUT's
config file is res://.gutconfig.json; the default test root is res://test;
C# suites use the [TestSuite] attribute on a plain class. Framework
detection, the headless and CI sections and the gotchas are new.

references/gut.md and references/gdunit4.md are new, written from the
official GUT docs (bitwes/Gut @ v9.7.1, aeb5d4f3f7f0a6c9b5e178876d6c99b791fda605,
MIT) and gdUnit4 docs and code (godot-gdunit-labs/gdUnit4 @ v6.2.2,
0127a55f4543dfc24746f6e5c7ba6f94105d51f2, MIT;
gdUnit4-action @ v1.3.2, MIT), not from GodotPrompter. No text was copied
from those projects; API names and option lists are facts checked against
their sources on 2026-10-17.
